@ Foldable, fold, size, all, any, none, elem, intercalate, foldMap, reverse, sortBy, sort

~ "Setoid" Setoid, equal
~ "Monoid" Monoid, empty
~ "Applicative" Applicative, append, prepend
~ "Ord" Ord, lt, lte
~ "Arithmetic" add, sub, inc
~ "Logical" and, or, not
~ "Semigroup" concat
~ "Filterable" filter

.. fold walks from the left. The initial value sits under the quotation.
.. size, all, any, none, elem, intercalate, foldMap and reverse are in Words/Fold.
.. sort and sortBy are in Words/Sort.
.. size counts with Num. Importing Num here cycles through Option.
& Foldable f
  .. Walk from the left. The initial value sits under the quotation.
  fold ( (f a) b (b a -- b) -- b )

? "fold" < 3 > [ < 1 2 > 0 [ add ] fold ]

. ..................................................................................................

.. How many elements. An empty structure is 0.
: size ( Foldable f => (f a) -- Num )
  Array -> size_array
  _ -> 0 [ drop inc ] fold

: foreign size_array ( (Array a) -- Num )

? "size of empty" < 0 > [ <> size ]
? "size of three" < 3 > [ < 1 2 3 > size ]

................................................................................................

.. True when every element suits the quotation. An empty structure is true.
: all ( Foldable f => (f a) (a -- Bool) -- Bool )
  Array _ -> all_array
  _ _ -> [ call and ] cons
          true swap fold

: foreign all_array ( (Array a) (a -- Bool) -- Bool )

? "all of empty" < true > [ <> [ drop false ] all ]
? "all holds" < true > [ < 1 1 > [ 1 equal ] all ]
? "all fails" < false > [ < 1 2 > [ 1 equal ] all ]

................................................................................................

.. True when one element suits the quotation. An empty structure is false.
: any ( Foldable f => (f a) (a -- Bool) -- Bool )
  Array _ -> any_array
  _ _ -> [ call or ] cons
          false swap fold

: foreign any_array ( (Array a) (a -- Bool) -- Bool )

? "any of empty" < false > [ <> [ drop true ] any ]
? "any holds" < true > [ < 0 1 > [ 1 equal ] any ]
? "any fails" < false > [ < 0 0.25 > [ 1 equal ] any ]

................................................................................................

.. True when no element suits the quotation. An empty structure is true.
: none ( Foldable f => (f a) (a -- Bool) -- Bool )
  any not

? "none of empty" < true > [ <> [ drop true ] none ]
? "none holds" < true > [ < 0 0.25 > [ 1 equal ] none ]
? "none fails" < false > [ < 0 1 > [ 1 equal ] none ]

................................................................................................

.. True when the upper value equals some element.
: elem ( Setoid a, Foldable f => (f a) a -- Bool )
  [ equal ] cons any

? "elem" < true > [ < 1 2 > 2 elem ]
? "elem empty" < false > [ < 1 > [ drop false ] filter 1 elem ]
? "elem hits" < true > [ < "a" "b" "c" > "c" elem ]
? "elem misses" < false > [ < "a" "b" "c" > "x" elem ]

................................................................................................

.. The pieces joined, with the separator between them. An empty structure is empty.
: intercalate ( Monoid m, Foldable f => (f m) m -- m )
  [ step ] cons emptyStore swap
  fold value>>

.. The first piece has not been joined yet. held is the monoid so far.
; Store m = Store empty : Bool, value : m

: emptyStore ( Monoid m => -- ( Store m ) )
  true empty Store

.. The next piece. The first piece is copied. Later pieces follow the separator.
: step ( Monoid m => (Store m) m m -- (Store m) ) . store item sep
  swap rot . sep item store
  [ value>> ] [ empty>> ] bi . sep item value empty
  [ unrot ] dip . value sep item empty
  [ swap drop ] [ concat ] if
  concat false swap Store

? "intercalate empty" < "" > [ <> ", " intercalate ]
? "intercalate strings" < "foo, bar, baz" > [ < "foo" "bar" "baz" > ", " intercalate ]
? "intercalate one" < "foo" > [ < "foo" > ", " intercalate ]
? "intercalate arrays" < < 1 0 0 2 3 > > [ < < 1 > < 2 3 > > < 0 0 > intercalate ]

................................................................................................

.. Concat each result, starting from empty.
: foldMap ( Monoid m, Foldable f => (f a) (a -- m) -- m )
  empty swap [ call concat ] cons fold

................................................................................................

.. The elements in the opposite order.
: reverse ( Applicative f, Foldable f, Monoid (f a) => (f a) -- (f a) )
  Array -> reverse_array
  _ -> empty [ prepend ] fold

: foreign reverse_array ( (Array a) -- (Array a) )

? "reverse" < < 3 2 1 > > [ < 1 2 3 > reverse ]
? "reverse one" < < 1 > > [ < 1 > reverse ]

................................................................................................

.. The elements ordered by the quotation, using lte on each result.
.. An equal result keeps the earlier element.
: sortBy ( Ord b, Applicative f, Foldable f, Monoid (f a) => (f a) (a -- b) -- (f a) )
  [ keyed ] cons <> swap fold
  [ compareKeyed ] sort_array
  empty [ item>> append ] fold

; Keyed a b = Keyed idx: Num, item : a, key : b

.. The rank array with this element and its key.
: keyed ( (Array (Keyed a b)) a (a -- b) -- (Array (Keyed a b)) )
  dupd call [ dup size ] dip2 Keyed append

: foreign sort_array ( ( Array a ) ( a a -- Num ) -- ( Array a ) )

: compareKeyed ( Ord b => ( Keyed a b ) ( Keyed a b ) -- Num )
  dup2 [ key>> ] bia lte
  [ dup2 [ key>> ] bia swap lte
    [ [ idx>> ] bia sub ] [ drop2 -1  ] if
  ] [ drop2 1 ] if


: foreign length_str ( Str -- Num )

? "sortBy length" < < "red" "blue" "green" > > [ < "red" "green" "blue" > [ length_str ] sortBy ]
? "sortBy keeps an earlier tie" < < "black" "white" > > [ < "black" "white" > [ length_str ] sortBy ]
? "sortBy keeps a later tie" < < "white" "black" > > [ < "white" "black" > [ length_str ] sortBy ]
? "sortBy keeps separated ties" < < "red" "blue" "green" "black" > > [ < "green" "red" "blue" "black" > [ length_str ] sortBy ]
? "sortBy empty" < <> > [ <> [ length_str ] sortBy ]
? "sortBy one" < < "red" > > [ < "red" > [ length_str ] sortBy ]

................................................................................................

.. The elements ordered by lte. An equal element keeps the earlier place.
: sort ( Ord a, Applicative f, Foldable f, Monoid (f a) => (f a) -- (f a) )
  [] sortBy

? "sort numbers" < < 1 2 3 > > [ < 3 1 2 > sort ]
? "sort reversed" < < 1 2 3 > > [ < 3 2 1 > sort ]
? "sort strings" < < "a" "b" "c" > > [ < "c" "a" "b" > sort ]
? "sort empty" < <> > [ < 1 > [ drop false ] filter sort ]
? "sort one" < < 1 > > [ < 1 > sort ]

. ..................................................................................................

# Foldable Array
  fold = fold_array

: foreign fold_array ( a b. (Array a) b (b a -- b) -- b )
